      "heading": {
        "hinglish": "8. Summary (Ab Tak Humne Kya Seekha)",
        "english": "8. Summary"
      },
      "body": {
        "hinglish": "Is article mein humne union aur enum ko poori tarah samjha:\n- **Union mein saare members ek hi memory share karte hain:** Union ka size sabse bade member ke barabar hota hai, aur ek member ko likhne se doosre member ki value badal jati hai.\n- **Hamesha wahi member padho jo sabse aakhir mein likha gaya tha:** Doosre member ko padhna wahi bytes ko galat roop mein padhna hai. Safe tareeka hai ek tag variable rakhna jo bataye ki kaun sa member active hai.\n- **Enum numbers ko naam deta hai:** `enum Day { MON, TUE, WED };` mein `MON` `0`, `TUE` `1` aur `WED` `2` hota hai. Custom values bhi di ja sakti hain, aur uske baad wali values apne aap badhti hain.\n- **Enum class zyada safe hai:** Uske naam scope ke andar band rehte hain aur woh apne aap `int` mein nahi badalta — convert karna ho toh `static_cast<int>` likho.\n- **Switch aur enum best friends hain:** `switch` mein `case WED:` likhne se code padhne layak banta hai, `case 2:` likhne se nahi.\n\nAgle article mein hum typedef aur using seekhenge — lambi type names ko chhota nickname dena aur apne khud ke type aliases banana.",
        "english": "In this article, we fully understood union and enum:\n- **In a union, all members share the same memory:** The size of a union equals its largest member, and writing one member changes the value of the other member.\n- **Always read the member written most recently:** Reading another member means reading the same bytes in the wrong form. The safe way is to keep a tag variable that says which member is active.\n- **An enum gives names to numbers:** In `enum Day { MON, TUE, WED };`, `MON` is `0`, `TUE` is `1` and `WED` is `2`. Custom values can be given too, and the values after them increase automatically.\n- **An enum class is safer:** Its names stay locked inside their scope and it never converts to `int` by itself — to convert, write `static_cast<int>`.\n- **Switch and enum are best friends:** Writing `case WED:` in a switch makes code readable; writing `case 2:` does not.\n\nIn the next article, we will learn typedef and using — giving short nicknames to long type names and creating your own type aliases."
      }
