      "body": {
        "hinglish": "Is article mein humne typedef aur using ko poori tarah samjha:\n- **Alias ek hi type ka doosra naam hai:** `typedef long long ll;` aur `using Marks = int;` dono naye naam banate hain, naya type nahi. Compiler ke liye alias aur asli type ek hi hain.\n- **Using modern aur zyada powerful hai:** Uska syntax seedha hai (`using NayaNaam = PuranaType;`) aur woh templates ke saath kaam karta hai — typedef templates ke saath kaam nahi karta.\n- **Pointer typedef trap:** `typedef int* IntPtr;` ke baad `IntPtr a, b;` mein dono pointer bante hain, jabki `int* a, b;` mein sirf `a` pointer hota hai.\n- **Alias compile time par kaam karta hai:** Compiler har alias ko uske asli type se badal deta hai, isiliye alias ka koi runtime cost nahi hota.\n- **Ek jagah badlaav, har jagah asar:** Alias ke peeche wala type badalne se poora program apne aap naye type par chal padta hai.\n\nAgle article mein hum new aur delete seekhenge — runtime par heap memory lena aur wapas karna, aur memory leak se kaise bacha jata hai.",
        "english": "In this article, we fully understood typedef and using:\n- **An alias is a second name for the same type:** Both `typedef long long ll;` and `using Marks = int;` create new names, not new types. For the compiler, the alias and the real type are one and the same.\n- **Using is modern and more powerful:** Its syntax is straightforward (`using NewName = OldType;`) and it works with templates — typedef does not work with templates.\n- **The pointer typedef trap:** After `typedef int* IntPtr;`, both variables in `IntPtr a, b;` become pointers, while in `int* a, b;` only `a` is a pointer.\n- **An alias works at compile time:** The compiler replaces every alias with its real type, so an alias has zero runtime cost.\n- **One change in one place, effect everywhere:** Changing the type behind an alias makes the whole program run on the new type by itself.\n\nIn the next article, we will learn new and delete — taking heap memory at runtime, giving it back, and how to avoid memory leaks."
      }
