        "hinglish": "### Worked Example 1 (chaaron containers) ka dry run:\n- **Stack:** push 10 -> `[10]`, top = 10. push 20 -> `[10, 20]`, top = 20. push 30 -> `[10, 20, 30]`, top = 30. Print: `Stack top: 30`. pop() -> `[10, 20]`. Print: `Stack top after pop: 20`.\n- **Queue:** push 10 -> `[10]`, push 20 -> `[10, 20]`, push 30 -> `[10, 20, 30]`. front = 10, back = 30. Print: `Queue front: 10, back: 30`. pop() -> `[20, 30]`. Print: `Queue front after pop: 20`.\n- **Deque:** push_back(20) -> `[20]`. push_front(10) -> `[10, 20]`. push_back(30) -> `[10, 20, 30]`. Print: `Deque: 10 20 30`.\n\n---\n\n### Worked Example 2 (Balanced Brackets) ka dry run — string `\"{[()]}\"`:\n- **Char `{`:** Opening bracket — push. Stack: `[{]`.\n- **Char `[`:** Opening bracket — push. Stack: `[{, []`.\n- **Char `(`:** Opening bracket — push. Stack: `[{, [, (]`.\n- **Char `)`:** Closing bracket — top dekho: `(` hai, jo `)` ka match hai. Pop karo. Stack: `[{, []`.\n- **Char `]`:** Closing bracket — top dekho: `[` hai, jo `]` ka match hai. Pop karo. Stack: `[{]`.\n- **Char `}`:** Closing bracket — top dekho: `{` hai, jo `}` ka match hai. Pop karo. Stack: khaali.\n- **Aakhir mein stack khaali hai** — isiliye `{[()]}` balanced hai, result `1`.\n\n### String `\"{[(])}\"` ka dry run (kyun unbalanced hai):\n- `{` push -> `[{]`. `[` push -> `[{, []`. `(` push -> `[{, [, (]`.\n- **Char `]`:** Closing bracket — top dekho: `(` hai, par `]` ka match `[` hota hai, `(` nahi! **Mismatch** — turant false return karo. Stack ki baaki checking ruk jaati hai. Result `0`.",
        "english": "### Dry run of Worked Example 1 (all four containers):\n- **Stack:** push 10 -> `[10]`, top = 10. push 20 -> `[10, 20]`, top = 20. push 30 -> `[10, 20, 30]`, top = 30. Print: `Stack top: 30`. pop() -> `[10, 20]`. Print: `Stack top after pop: 20`.\n- **Queue:** push 10 -> `[10]`, push 20 -> `[10, 20]`, push 30 -> `[10, 20, 30]`. front = 10, back = 30. Print: `Queue front: 10, back: 30`. pop() -> `[20, 30]`. Print: `Queue front after pop: 20`.\n- **Deque:** push_back(20) -> `[20]`. push_front(10) -> `[10, 20]`. push_back(30) -> `[10, 20, 30]`. Print: `Deque: 10 20 30`.\n\n---\n\n### Dry run of Worked Example 2 (Balanced Brackets) — string `\"{[()]}\"`:\n- **Char `{`:** Opening bracket — push. Stack: `[{]`.\n- **Char `[`:** Opening bracket — push. Stack: `[{, []`.\n- **Char `(`:** Opening bracket — push. Stack: `[{, [, (]`.\n- **Char `)`:** Closing bracket — look at the top: it is `(`, which matches `)`. Pop it. Stack: `[{, []`.\n- **Char `]`:** Closing bracket — look at the top: it is `[`, which matches `]`. Pop it. Stack: `[{]`.\n- **Char `}`:** Closing bracket — look at the top: it is `{`, which matches `}`. Pop it. Stack: empty.\n- **At the end the stack is empty** — so `{[()]}` is balanced, result `1`.\n\n### Dry run of the string `\"{[(])}\"` (why it is unbalanced):\n- `{` push -> `[{]`. `[` push -> `[{, []`. `(` push -> `[{, [, (]`.\n- **Char `]`:** Closing bracket — look at the top: it is `(`, but the match for `]` is `[`, not `(`! **Mismatch** — return false immediately. The rest of the checking stops. Result `0`."
